---
import LegalLayout from "@/layouts/LegalLayout.astro";
import { legal } from "@/lib/legal";
---

<LegalLayout
  title="Terms of Service"
  description={`Terms of Service for ${legal.brandName}.`}
  heading="Terms of Service"
  eyebrow="AGB · Nutzungsbedingungen"
>
  <p>
    These Terms of Service (“Terms”) form a binding agreement between you
    (“Customer”, “you”, “Merchant”) and <strong>{legal.legalName}</strong>
    (“{legal.brandName}”, “we”, “us”) governing access to and use of the
    DeclineGuard website, dashboard, APIs, and related services (the
    “Service”). By creating an account, connecting a store, or otherwise using
    the Service, you agree to these Terms and our
    <a href="/legal/privacy">Privacy Policy</a>. If you use the Service on
    behalf of a company, you represent that you have authority to bind that
    company.
  </p>
  <p>
    Related documents: <a href="/legal/dpa">Data Processing Agreement</a>,
    <a href="/legal/impressum">Impressum</a>,
    <a href="/legal/cookies">Cookie Notice</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>1. The Service</h2>
  <p>
    DeclineGuard is a B2B software service that helps Lemon Squeezy merchants
    recover failed subscription renewals by detecting relevant webhook events
    and sending branded transactional recovery email sequences with a link for
    the end customer to update payment via Lemon Squeezy.
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>We do not process or store payment card numbers.</li>
    <li>Payment collection from end customers is handled by Lemon Squeezy / the customer’s payment methods — not by DeclineGuard as a payment facilitator for those cards.</li>
    <li>We are not a bank, payment institution, or substitute for Lemon Squeezy’s merchant agreement.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>2. Eligibility &amp; accounts</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>You must be at least 18 and able to form a binding contract.</li>
    <li>The Service is offered to businesses / merchants (B2B), not consumers for private purposes. If you are a consumer under EU/German law despite the B2B positioning, mandatory consumer protections remain unaffected where they cannot be waived.</li>
    <li>You must provide accurate registration information and keep credentials confidential. You are responsible for activity under your account.</li>
    <li>We may refuse, suspend, or terminate accounts that violate these Terms or pose risk (fraud, abuse, legal risk).</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>3. Lemon Squeezy connection</h2>
  <p>
    To use core features you must connect a Lemon Squeezy store using an API key
    (or other credentials we support) and ensure webhooks can reach us. You
    represent that you are authorised to connect that store and to process your
    customers’ data as described in the DPA.
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>You must keep API keys secret; revoke keys if compromised.</li>
    <li>You remain solely responsible for your Lemon Squeezy account, products, pricing, taxes, refunds, chargebacks, and compliance with Lemon Squeezy’s terms.</li>
    <li>We may store an encrypted copy of credentials and limited store metadata to operate the Service.</li>
    <li>Disconnecting a store may delete associated recovery records as implemented in the product; export anything you need first.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>4. Plans, fees &amp; founding terms</h2>
  <h3>4.1 Free plan</h3>
  <p>
    On the Free plan, the Service is offered at <strong>$0 per month</strong> with a
    recovery success fee of <strong>10% of amounts recovered</strong> where a
    recovery is attributed to DeclineGuard under Section 4.3. Free includes
    <strong>100 recovery emails per month</strong> and <strong>one Lemon Squeezy
    store</strong>, with optional add-ons as shown on the pricing page (extra
    email packs and one-time fees for additional stores). We may limit Free
    enrolment at any time for new customers.
  </p>
  <h3>4.2 Pro plan</h3>
  <p>
    Pro is marketed at <strong>$29.99 per month</strong> (or such price as shown
    at checkout / in-app) with a <strong>4% recovery fee</strong>, and includes
    higher email volume, unlimited stores, removal of DeclineGuard attribution
    from emails, and other features described on the pricing page at the time of
    purchase. Optional email overage packs may apply as shown on the pricing
    page. Features may evolve; material downgrades to paid plans will be handled
    reasonably (notice or pro‑rata credit/refund where required by law).
  </p>
  <h3>4.3 When a recovery fee is owed</h3>
  <p>
    Unless we expressly agree otherwise in writing, a Free-plan recovery fee is
    owed only when:
  </p>
  <ol>
    <li>a failed-payment event for a subscription is ingested by DeclineGuard for your connected store; and</li>
    <li>DeclineGuard has started the recovery sequence for that failure (first email queued/sent according to our systems); and</li>
    <li>we receive a corresponding recovery / success event (or equivalent confirmation) attributable to that subscription/failure within our attribution window of <strong>[ATTRIBUTION WINDOW: e.g. 30 days]</strong>.</li>
  </ol>
  <p>
    If the customer pays successfully <em>before</em> our first recovery email
    for that failure is sent, no DeclineGuard recovery fee is owed for that
    event. We calculate fees on the recovered amount and currency reported by
    Lemon Squeezy events (converted for invoicing if needed using a reasonable
    market rate or our payment provider’s rate).
  </p>
  <h3>4.4 Invoicing &amp; payment of our fees</h3>
  <p>
    Fees may be collected via invoice, card/SEPA checkout, Lemon Squeezy, or
    another processor we designate. You authorise us to invoice and collect
    amounts due. Late amounts may accrue interest at the statutory rate and/or
    reasonable collection costs where permitted. We may suspend the Service for
    non-payment after notice.
  </p>
  <h3>4.5 Taxes</h3>
  <p>
    Fees are exclusive of VAT and similar taxes unless stated otherwise. If VAT
    applies, it will be added as required. You are responsible for taxes on your
    own sales to end customers.
  </p>
  <h3>4.6 Price changes</h3>
  <p>
    We may change prices for renewals or new subscriptions with reasonable
    prior notice. Continued use after the effective date constitutes acceptance
    unless you cancel before the change applies.
  </p>

  <h2>5. Your responsibilities</h2>
  <p>You agree to:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Use the Service only for lawful business purposes and in compliance with GDPR/DSGVO, ePrivacy, UWG/unfair competition, CAN-SPAM/CASL where applicable, and your contracts with customers.</li>
    <li>Ensure you have a valid legal basis to send recovery emails to end customers and that content is accurate and not misleading.</li>
    <li>Configure brand, from-name, reply-to, and support details correctly; you are responsible for customer replies to those addresses.</li>
    <li>Not use the Service to spam, phish, harass, or send unlawful content.</li>
    <li>Not reverse engineer, abuse rate limits, probe for vulnerabilities without authorisation, or resell the Service except as we agree in writing.</li>
    <li>Not upload malware or infringing content.</li>
    <li>Promptly notify us of security incidents involving your API keys or unauthorised account use.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>6. Email content &amp; brand licence</h2>
  <p>
    You grant us a non-exclusive licence to use your store name, logos, brand
    colours, and related assets solely to send recovery emails and display them
    in your dashboard as part of the Service. You warrant you have rights to
    those assets. Free-plan emails may include DeclineGuard attribution.
  </p>

  <h2>7. Data protection</h2>
  <p>
    Each party shall comply with applicable data protection law. For
    end-customer personal data processed in providing the Service, the
    <a href="/legal/dpa">DPA</a> applies and prevails on processing terms in
    case of conflict. You are controller; we are processor for that data.
  </p>

  <h2>8. Intellectual property</h2>
  <p>
    We and our licensors own the Service, software, designs, and DeclineGuard
