    stated, and to the maximum extent permitted by law, the Service is provided
    “as is” and “as available” without warranties of uninterrupted operation,
    error-free recovery rates, or fitness for a particular purpose. We do not
    guarantee any specific recovery percentage or revenue outcome.
  </p>

  <h2>12. Liability</h2>
  <p>
    Nothing in these Terms excludes liability that cannot be limited under
    applicable law (e.g. intent, gross negligence, injury to life/body/health,
    fraud, or mandatory product liability).
  </p>
  <p>
    Subject to the foregoing, our aggregate liability arising out of or related
    to the Service in any twelve-month period is limited to the greater of
    (a) fees you paid us for the Service in that period, or (b)
    <strong>€100</strong>. We are not liable for indirect, incidental, special,
    consequential, or lost-profit damages, loss of goodwill, or lost data, except
    where caused by our intent or gross negligence or where mandatory law
    provides otherwise.
  </p>
  <p>
    You are responsible for verifying recovery emails and payment links before
    relying on them in production; maintain your own customer support processes.
  </p>

  <h2>13. Indemnity</h2>
  <p>
    You will defend and indemnify us against claims, damages, and reasonable
    costs arising from: (a) your content, products, or customer relationships;
    (b) your misuse of the Service or violation of law; (c) your failure to have
    a lawful basis to contact end customers; or (d) disputes between you and
    your customers or Lemon Squeezy — except to the extent caused by our breach
    of these Terms or the DPA.
  </p>

  <h2>14. Suspension &amp; termination</h2>
  <p>
    You may stop using the Service and request account closure by contacting
    {legal.supportEmail}. We may suspend or terminate for breach, legal risk,
    non-payment, or extended inactivity after notice where reasonable. Upon
    termination, your licence ends; Sections that by nature should survive
    (fees owed, IP, liability, indemnity, governing law) survive. Data handling
    after termination follows the Privacy Policy and DPA.
  </p>

  <h2>15. Changes to the Service or Terms</h2>
  <p>
    We may modify the Service and these Terms. For material adverse changes to
    Terms, we will provide notice (email or in-app) at least
    <strong>14 days</strong> in advance where practicable. If you do not agree,
    you must stop using the Service and may cancel. Continued use after the
    effective date constitutes acceptance, except where mandatory law requires
    explicit consent.
  </p>

  <h2>16. Export &amp; sanctions</h2>
  <p>
    You may not use the Service if you are subject to sanctions or in a
    prohibited jurisdiction under applicable EU/US/UK export or sanctions laws.
  </p>

  <h2>17. Governing law &amp; venue</h2>
  <p>
    These Terms are governed by {legal.governingLaw}, excluding conflict-of-law
    rules. Exclusive venue is {legal.venue}, subject to mandatory venues for
    consumers if applicable. The UN CISG does not apply.
  </p>

  <h2>18. Miscellaneous</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>These Terms plus the DPA, Privacy Policy, and any order form are the entire agreement regarding the Service.</li>
    <li>If a provision is unenforceable, the remainder stays in effect.</li>
    <li>Failure to enforce is not a waiver.</li>
    <li>You may not assign without our consent; we may assign to an affiliate or successor.</li>
    <li>Notices: {legal.legalEmail} / {legal.supportEmail}; we may notice you via account email.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>19. Contact</h2>
